The third stage of the L1 reader, written in L1. It takes the syntax tree from parse.prog and builds the quoted form of the expression: the same value that Code.toValue gives for the Expr that the Luau reader builds. A quoted node is [tag args], with the tags of code.luau.
The names are resolved to indices, the forms are read as the Luau reader reads them, and the mutual desugaring is the same, so the output of this stage is the same expression for every program the Luau reader accepts. An error is a raised message.
---

---
